      "title": "T3e \u00b7 Preserve Rowan's chunky proportions; change pose only",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.5.1",
        "Node name for S&R": "TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus",
        "enableTabs": false,
        "tabWidth": 65,
        "tabXOffset": 10,
        "hasSecondTab": false,
        "secondTabText": "Send Back",
        "secondTabOffset": 80,
        "secondTabWidth": 65
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit only the pose and viewing angle of the exact character in the supplied image; do not redesign the character. Preserve EXACTLY the approved concept's chunky cute proportions and design: an oversized head well over one third of the total standing height, a very large rounded moss-green hood, extremely short stubby arms, a short torso, very short legs, large round hands, and oversized chunky boots. Keep the head large and the limbs short exactly as in the input image; do not shrink the head, lengthen the arms or legs, lengthen the torso, slim the body, or make the anatomy more realistic. Turn the character to face the camera straight on in a symmetrical full-body front view. Put both short arms straight out to opposite sides, perfectly horizontal at shoulder height, with straight elbows and open hands, palms down and fingers together; keep empty background between the arms and torso. Keep the legs straight with a small clear gap between the legs and feet, feet flat and pointing forward. Preserve the exact hood shape and single thick leaf sprout, dark-brown hair, simple face with black oval eyes and tiny mouth, cream long-sleeved tunic, honey-brown belt and shorts, chunky honey-brown boots, coral leaf emblem, original colours, soft hand-painted look and broad rounded shapes. No weapon, shield or held object; no cape, scarf, loose cloth or anything bridging body parts. Plain uniform light warm-gray background, soft even lighting, no ground shadow, no floor plane, no text, no extra objects, full body fully inside the frame with generous margin."
      ],
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
    },
